---
import "../styles/custom.css"
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro"
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro"
const title = 'About — Vectis Mail'
const description = 'Vectis Mail is the self-hosted email platform from Veltara Works — declarative YAML config, REST API, atomic updates. Built for developers and sysadmins.'
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<title>{title}</title>
	<meta name="description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
	<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
	<meta property="og:url" content="https://vectismail.com/about/" />
	<meta property="og:image" content="https://vectismail.com/og/default.png" />
	<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
	<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
	<meta property="og:image:alt" content="About Vectis Mail — built by Veltara Works" />
	<meta property="og:site_name" content="Vectis Mail" />
	<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
	<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
	<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
	<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://vectismail.com/og/default.png" />
	<meta name="theme-color" content="#0C0C0D" />
	<link rel="canonical" href="https://vectismail.com/about/" />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "Organization",
		"name": "Vectis Mail",
		"url": "https://vectismail.com",
		"logo": "https://vectismail.com/brand/logos/vectis-mail-logo-white.webp",
		"description": "Self-hosted email platform with declarative config, sending API, and enterprise features. A product of Veltara Works.",
		"parentOrganization": {
			"@type": "Organization",
			"name": "Veltara Works",
			"url": "https://veltaraworks.com"
		},
		"sameAs": [
			"https://github.com/Veltara-Works/vectis",
			"https://validonx.com",
			"https://pharlux.com",
			"https://veltaraworks.com"
		]
	})} />
</head>
<body class="marketing-page">
	<SiteNav />

	<main>

	<section class="section" style="max-width: 700px;">
		<h1>About Vectis Mail&trade;</h1>
		<p style="color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem;">
			Vectis Mail is built and operated by <strong style="color: var(--sl-color-white);">Veltara Works</strong>, an independent software company based in Australia and founded by <strong style="color: var(--sl-color-white);">Ian Holt</strong>. Email is critical infrastructure, and we run it that way: when you need help you reach the people who build and operate the platform directly — not an outsourced first-response tier reading from a script.
		</p>
		<p style="color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
			The reason Vectis Mail exists: email is critical infrastructure, yet most teams hand it to providers they can't inspect, can't customise, and can't audit. Vectis Mail is the alternative — a production-grade self-hosted mail server you can deploy with one command, manage through a REST API and admin UI, and is designed to grow with you as your needs change.
		</p>
		<p style="color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
			Two principles we'll put in writing. <strong style="color: var(--sl-color-white);">No lock-in — and no lock-out:</strong> Vectis Mail is self-hosted and source-available, and every release converts to Apache 2.0 four years on, so your mail runs on infrastructure you own and control — independent of us. Pro's licensing backend is a configurable endpoint — <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ValidonX</a> is the default we operate, not a hardwired dependency — and no mail or message data ever passes through it. <strong style="color: var(--sl-color-white);">We run on it ourselves:</strong> every domain Veltara Works operates already lives on Vectis Mail — <a href="/notes/dogfooding-our-own-email/" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">here's exactly how</a>.
		</p>
		<p style="color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
			Vectis Mail sits under the <strong style="color: var(--sl-color-white);">Veltara Works</strong> umbrella, alongside <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent); font-weight: 700;">ValidonX</a> (licensing, billing, and identity) and <a href="https://pharlux.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent); font-weight: 700;">Pharlux</a> (single-binary OpenTelemetry observability) — a portfolio of infrastructure tools for operators who want full control of their stack. Together they form an operations foundation for self-hosted infrastructure.
		</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 3rem;">The Veltara Works Ecosystem</h2>
		<div class="feature-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Vectis Mail</h3>
				<p>Self-hosted email platform. Inbound/outbound mail, sending API, webhooks, admin dashboard.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3><a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-white); text-decoration: none;">ValidonX</a></h3>
				<p>Licensing, billing, and identity platform. Subscription management, feature gating, usage metering. <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">Learn more &rarr;</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3><a href="https://pharlux.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-white); text-decoration: none;">Pharlux</a></h3>
				<p>Single-binary OpenTelemetry observability. Replaces the LGTM stack with one Rust binary &mdash; metrics and logs on a single VPS, no Docker, no ClickHouse. <a href="https://pharlux.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">Learn more &rarr;</a></p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<p class="page-meta">Last updated <time datetime="2026-06-14">14 June 2026</time></p>

	</main>

	<SiteFooter />
</body>
</html>
